%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 320 200
%%Title: Fractal mountains
% Status: draft
% fractal_clouds#1: ridged-fBm mountains under a ray-marched cumulus layer,
% one ray per pixel. Preview: DPI=144 scripts/render.sh -D Res=0.25.
% Large: DPI=288 scripts/render.sh -D ErN=1024 -D ErDrops=240000 (1280x800, ~40 min).

/Seed where { pop } { /Seed 5 def } ifelse
/AA where { pop } { /AA true def } ifelse          % antialias depth edges (before fc_render.ps loads)
/Pitch where { pop } { /Pitch 0 def } ifelse
/Yaw where { pop } { /Yaw 10 def } ifelse          % layered ridges toward the peaks
/SunDir where { pop } { /SunDir [ -0.62 0.40 0.62 ] def } ifelse    % low, front-left of the view
/CloudLo where { pop } { /CloudLo 60 def /CloudHi 88 def } ifelse
/CoverAmp where { pop } { /CoverAmp 0.45 def } ifelse      % clouds in groups
/HazeDist where { pop } { /HazeDist 400 def } ifelse      % thicker air than the default
/Threshold where { pop } { /Threshold 0.57 def } ifelse
/CamLift where { pop } { /CamLift 0.72 def } ifelse  % camera height, as a fraction of the tallest peaks

(lib/fc_landscape.ps) run
320 200 fc-landscape
showpage
